From 5134e20a73429468ec5bf80b4a4fb9d55e962a80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iitimii <timiiowolabi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 12:16:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] S3.4: residency wiring, ledger log, tier-switch
 choreography, sticky demote

Wires the weight residency manager into llama-duo, per tier.

- duo flags mirroring common: --stream-weights, --max-ram-mib, --prefetch-layers,
  --pin-budget, --stream-reserve-mib, --disk-gbps. All inert without
  --stream-weights, so the no-flag baselines are byte-identical.
- STREAMED tiers load with model_params::stream_weights, get a manager built
  between the load and the context (cb_eval install), and are parked (suspended)
  unless they are the active tier.
- Cross-model ledger: mlock_front_mib from a new llama_model_mlock_bytes()
  accessor (the lock range, header-inclusive), resident_other_mib from the other
  tiers' resident weights plus every other tier's KV, reserve_mib from this tier's
  own KV plus a compute/slack constant. Per-tier KV is computed from GGUF metadata
  (attention KV + Gated-DeltaNet recurrent state, checkpoint-doubled contexts
  itemized), because the ledger charges tiers for contexts that do not exist yet.
- Sticky demote: if the mid tier's ledger refuses with easy resident, easy is
  demoted to streamed once, loudly; an explicit --tier-policy easy=resident
  refuses to start instead. Streamed tiers load first under --stream-weights so
  the decision precedes easy's load.
- switch_to(): suspend the outgoing tier (bulk evict incl. pins), trace, then
  resume_async the incoming one at the DECISION point so the activation overlaps
  the front's opener extension. Sites: route, conf escalation, easy answering,
  verify, codraft pair.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5
